WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.630 align:start position:0%
 
welcome back to ctm  our series of more perfect union aims to  show that what unites us as americans  is far greater than what divides us this  morning we're going to do something a  little different  as the world prepares to say goodbye to  one of the most difficult years we've  had in history  we asked spiritual leaders for their  thoughts on unity and hope heading into  2021.  so we spoke with imam omar suleiman  founder of the yakin institute for  islamic research  roshi pat in keo o'hara a zen buddhist  teacher father james martin a jesuit  priest and author of the book learning  to pray  reverend jackie lewis senior minister at  middle collegiate church  rabbi rick jacobs president of the union  for reform judaism  and sanjida kausik  hindu who is an advisor at new york  university  20 20 has been a terrible year and it's  not surprising that people  would sometimes feel tempted to despair  but i like to remind people that those  feelings of despair  aren't coming from god that's not the  way that god works feelings of hope are  the only thing that keeps us going is  hope and firm  faith in god that everything that  happened even the losses that you have  suffered  is for a reason  the quran says that with every hardship  there is ease  and so when blessings are taken away  from us voluntarily or involuntarily  then we have a greater awareness of god  a greater awareness of self and a  greater awareness of other  and that's where we seek the greatest  growth  so my hope comes from the human will to  survive the tenacity and resilience of  human beings  in partnership with a holy other which  is how i think about god as a holy other  and in partnership together we make it  we just do  we rise up out of ashes and we talk  about it and we do new things together  love thy neighbor is one of those great  teachings in the hebrew bible  but it only is mentioned once love the  strangers mentioned 36 times why because  it's much  harder and as a buddhist what's  important to me is that we  recognize that we are interconnected  loving the stranger loving the one who's  different  that's where we anchor our lives on a  very different foundation and that's how  we overcome  the incredibly painful divisions of this  moment  listen with compassion realize  that on a fundamental level as two  humans  the person who thinks completely  differently than i do  is another human that we have that  connection and maybe  maybe it's just expressing a little  empathy but it's the beginning of a  bridge  rather than throwing a rock  i think one thing that we can all agree  on is the  the valor um and the heroism of our  health care professionals the example  that we've been given  by the caring people particularly in the  essentially the essential workers  you know the people that are running the  subways around here  as well as as the ones that are in  medical  frame those are our heroes sometimes in  our darkest moments we find our greatest  unity and  the greatest beauty in that unity comes  in the midst of that darkness  we know how to have our neighbors backs  we know how to  put sandbags along each other's houses  we know how to give each other groceries  and take care of each other's kids we do  know how to do it if we talk  more about what we have in common and  emphasize what we have in common i think  goodness  triumphs over evil every single time the  light triumphs over  darkness every single time so i would  hope that as we're finishing  2020 and saying good ribbons  that we enter 21 with the feeling of  each of us is responsible for shaping 21  to be  a year of healing a year of hope  a year of kindness but that we come  together  with a shared sense of building a more  just and compassionate world  [Music]  my fondest hope for 2021 as a vaccine  let's just be blunt  that's my biggest hope and that's what  i've been praying for i hope people can  have fun again  i think just to be able to be outside  and be with your friends and  hug one another i think everybody is in  need of fun  in 2021. as we turn our faces toward a  new year  i hope that you can feel  the wind of a spirit at your back  and that your face will turn up toward  the sun and you will  imagine all of the wounds of this year  as places in which strength will grow  that we will be better  tomorrow  [Music]  what are your wishes my wishes and i  think i mentioned this yesterday is that  i hope that what we've learned about the  importance of being connected to one  another to staying in touch with your  friends and family  more than we usually do that we we  really did that this year i did that  this year  i want that to continue past 2021 for  years to come  david um my my hope is for empathy you  know people say happy new year i wish  you health and wealth and  it's for empathy because i think empathy  is what drives  the best in all of us it's important to  have empathy and i i love what  uh imam omar suleiman said in our  darkest moments we find  our greatest unity that message  resonates always with me when things are  dark it's always darkest before the dawn  it's an important moment that piece was  produced by andy murlis and sergeant  josephson  really really wonderful we'll be right  back

